# Build-context exclusions for the SentinelAI image.
#
# Two jobs. First, keep the context small and the build cache stable - a
# large .git directory or a local .venv would be shipped to the daemon on
# every build and would invalidate the COPY layer on every commit.
#
# Second, and more importantly: nothing here should ever reach an image
# that may be published. Environment files, model data, and generated
# scan reports can all carry credentials or a detailed map of a private
# codebase. The Dockerfile copies only sentinelai-cli/, but these rules
# are what keep that safe even if the COPY is ever widened.
#
# Pattern note: .dockerignore patterns are anchored to the context root
# and do NOT recurse on their own - a bare `__pycache__/` would exclude
# only /__pycache__, leaving sentinelai-cli/sentinelai/__pycache__/ in
# the context. Anything that can appear at any depth is therefore written
# with a `**/` prefix.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore's intent but is deliberately a separate file: git and
# Docker exclude for different reasons, and a file can be legitimately
# committed yet still have no business inside an image (tests, docs, the
# deliberately-vulnerable benchmark fixture).

# --- Version control -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Python caches and build artifacts -------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/*.so
**/build/
**/dist/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.egg
**/.eggs/
**/wheels/

# --- Virtual environments --------------------------------------------------
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/ENV/
**/env/
**/.tox/
**/.nox/

# --- Test and tooling caches ----------------------------------------------
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/

# --- Environment files and secrets ----------------------------------------
# Never build a credential into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.envrc
**/secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/credentials.json

# --- Local model data ------------------------------------------------------
# No model weights are bundled: AI enrichment reaches a separately
# configured Ollama host. These rules keep a local download from being
# swept into the context by accident.
**/.ollama/
**/models/
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
**/*.pt
**/*.onnx

# --- Generated scan output and reports ------------------------------------
# Reproducible by re-running the CLI; never source, and potentially a
# detailed map of a private codebase.
**/scan-result*.json
**/sentinelai-cli-scan*.json
**/ai-latency-run*.json
**/sentinelai-report*.html
**/sentinelai-report*.md
**/sentinelai-results*.sarif
**/*.sarif
**/report.json
**/report.md
**/report.html
**/sentinelai-output/

# --- Editor and OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/.idea/
**/.vscode/
**/*.swp

# --- Not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------------
# The image runs the CLI. It does not run the test suite, render the
# docs, or scan the deliberately-vulnerable benchmark fixture - shipping
# that fixture into an image would plant known-vulnerable files and fake
# credentials inside it.
sentinelai-manual-test/
sentinelai-cli/tests/
sentinelai-cli/docs/
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
